  "where": "Recognition Schemes live in data/recognition/<destination>.json, one file per Destination, named for the Destination rather than for the publication. A Destination has at most one of these and the engine reaches it from a requirement that names its scale, so the filename is the lookup and nothing has to index it. It is deliberately NOT a field on the Destination record: a Destination record is country context a student reads, this is a translation table the engine executes, and the two change on completely different clocks — the handbook is reissued every March, the country profile is not.",
